WEBVTT

1
00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:49.708
<b>Here Krishna speaks of those</b>
<b>people who are confused,</b>

2
00:00:49.708 --> 00:00:52.541
<b>whose thinking is limited.</b>

3
00:00:52.541 --> 00:00:53.875
<b>Krishna explains</b>

4
00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:56.416
<b>that such people are filled with desires,</b>

5
00:00:56.416 --> 00:00:59.750
<b>they perform every action only for its rewards,</b>

6
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.666
<b>and consider heaven alone</b>
<b>as their ultimate goal.</b>

7
00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:07.041
<b>Without fully understanding the Vedas,</b>

8
00:01:07.041 --> 00:01:13.166
<b>these people read and follow only </b>
<b>those parts within them that benefit them,</b>

9
00:01:13.166 --> 00:01:18.000
<b>They perform many religious rituals, </b>
<b>so that they may reap the rewards.</b>

10
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.875
<b>The truth is that these people</b>
<b>don't even know the Vedas,</b>

11
00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:24.583
<b>their thinking is limited</b>

12
00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:30.583
<b>Vedas</b>

13
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:33.125
<b>are an infinite ocean of knowledge.</b>

14
00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:35.916
<b>The Vedas are like a vast tree</b>

15
00:01:35.916 --> 00:01:38.458
<b>that bears all kinds of fruits,</b>

16
00:01:38.458 --> 00:01:41.000
<b>you will get whatever you seek.</b>

17
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.208
<b>Material pleasures,</b>

18
00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:43.083
<b>devotion,</b>

19
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:43.916
<b>liberation.</b>

20
00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:45.083
<b>Different people </b>

21
00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:48.208
<b>study the Vedas for different reasons.</b>

22
00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.875
<b>Here Krishna speaks of those people </b>

23
00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:54.541
<b>who seek only and </b>
<b>exclusively material pleasures,</b>

24
00:01:54.541 --> 00:01:56.666
<b>who desire indulgence and luxury.</b>

25
00:01:56.666 --> 00:01:59.708
<b>Krishna calls such people unwise.</b>

26
00:01:59.708 --> 00:02:01.875
<b>Why does Krishna say this?</b>

27
00:02:01.875 --> 00:02:05.750
<b>It is said that if your spectacles are red,</b>

28
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.166
<b>everything will appear red to you.</b>

29
00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:09.041
<b>Similarly,</b>

30
00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:11.791
<b>when these people study the Vedas,</b>

31
00:02:11.791 --> 00:02:16.166
<b>they are attracted to and see only those words</b>

32
00:02:16.166 --> 00:02:20.250
<b>that tell how to attain pleasures and luxuries,</b>

33
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.000
<b>what rituals should be performed for these.</b>

34
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.875
<b>These people become absorbed in only </b>
<b>these activities and religious ceremonies.</b>

35
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:33.583
<b>The biggest foolishness here is that by </b>
<b>reading only the self-serving portions,</b>

36
00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:36.833
<b>they begin to consider themselves </b>
<b>knowledgeable in the Vedas.</b>

37
00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:41.416
<b>The truth is that they don't have</b>
<b>true knowledge of the Vedas at all</b>

38
00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:44.125
<b>Pleasure, luxury, desire for rewards...</b>

39
00:02:44.125 --> 00:02:48.500
<b>the means to these are just a </b>
<b>very small part of the Vedas.</b>

40
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.541
<b>There is far higher and greater </b>
<b>knowledge within the Vedas,</b>

41
00:02:53.541 --> 00:02:55.375
<b>The Vedas also contain that knowledge</b>

42
00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:58.416
<b>which shows the difference </b>
<b>between materiality and soul,</b>

43
00:02:58.416 --> 00:03:02.708
<b>and suggests the path to realizing God.</b>

44
00:03:07.041 --> 00:03:14.291
<b>Often, people use religion</b>
<b>merely to fulfill their desires.</b>

45
00:03:14.291 --> 00:03:20.000
<b>They perform religious rituals</b>
<b>expecting rewards in return.</b>

46
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.916
<b>This isn't wrong</b>

47
00:03:21.916 --> 00:03:25.250
<b>rituals do yield fruits.</b>

48
00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.833
<b>But,</b>

49
00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:29.000
<b>the problem arises</b>

50
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:36.041
<b>when such people begin to view religion</b>
<b>through this narrow lens alone.</b>

51
00:03:36.041 --> 00:03:43.583
<b>They reduce religion to merely a</b>
<b>means of fulfilling their wishes.</b>

52
00:03:43.583 --> 00:03:49.458
<b>To the wise seeker who wishes to </b>
<b>grasp the true essence of religion,</b>

53
00:03:49.458 --> 00:03:55.791
<b>such people, their rituals, and </b>
<b>their grand displays all appear </b>

54
00:03:55.791 --> 00:03:59.500
<b>as mere pretense.</b>

55
00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:04.625
<b>Religion and the Vedas do </b>
<b>offer ways to fulfill desires.</b>

56
00:04:04.625 --> 00:04:13.166
<b>The error isn't in using religion to fulfill wishes</b>

57
00:04:13.166 --> 00:04:16.500
<b>the grave mistake occurs</b>

58
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.708
<b>when such people, based on</b>
<b>their limited knowledge,</b>

59
00:04:19.708 --> 00:04:27.250
<b>proclaim themselves as supreme scholars</b>
<b>of the Vedas and religion.</b>

60
00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:28.583
<b>Different people,</b>

61
00:04:28.583 --> 00:04:31.125
<b>different purposes.</b>

62
00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:33.708
<b>Material goals aren't wrong.</b>

63
00:04:33.708 --> 00:04:39.458
<b>Using religion to achieve these </b>
<b>goals isn't necessarily wrong either.</b>

64
00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:41.458
<b>But to possess incomplete knowledge</b>

65
00:04:41.458 --> 00:04:45.791
<b>and declare oneself all-knowing, </b>
<b>misleading others</b>

66
00:04:45.791 --> 00:04:48.833
<b>this is entirely inappropriate.</b>

67
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:52.250
<b>Now that you've embarked on this spiritual path,</b>

68
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.458
<b>remain aware.</b>

69
00:04:54.458 --> 00:04:56.166
<b>Different types of people,</b>

70
00:04:56.166 --> 00:04:58.000
<b>their various purposes,</b>

71
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:03.083
<b>their diverse religious understanding.</b>

72
00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:06.791
<b>Don't let all this confuse you.</b>

73
00:05:06.791 --> 00:05:10.500
<b>Simply walk forward with patience,</b>

74
00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:16.791
<b>and sincerely strive to understand </b>
<b>the true essence of religion.</b>

75
00:05:16.791 --> 00:05:23.125
<b>And remember, I am always here to help you.</b>

76
00:05:23.125 --> 00:05:24.583
<b>Keep moving forward.</b>

77
00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.791
<b>Often, people</b>

78
00:05:30.791 --> 00:05:40.458
<b>participate in religious ceremonies without </b>
<b>understanding their core meaning or true purpose.</b>

79
00:05:40.458 --> 00:05:46.833
<b>They do so based merely on a </b>
<b>superficial knowledge of scriptures.</b>

80
00:05:46.833 --> 00:05:50.250
<b>Since the perspective itself is flawed</b>

81
00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.083
<b>and the knowledge incomplete,</b>

82
00:05:52.083 --> 00:05:57.958
<b>even proper rituals fail to </b>
<b>yield complete benefits.</b>

83
00:05:57.958 --> 00:05:59.375
<b>For example</b>

84
00:05:59.375 --> 00:06:03.041
<b>charity is a noble deed.</b>

85
00:06:03.041 --> 00:06:04.375
<b>But if</b>

86
00:06:04.375 --> 00:06:08.083
<b>someone does it solely for prestige,</b>

87
00:06:08.083 --> 00:06:11.875
<b>then isn't the purpose itself misguided?</b>

88
00:06:11.875 --> 00:06:14.666
<b>How can one receive full benefits?</b>

89
00:06:14.666 --> 00:06:17.875
<b>The fundamental purpose of spiritual activities</b>

90
00:06:17.875 --> 00:06:21.083
<b>is to purify our consciousness.</b>

91
00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:21.875
<b>Yet</b>

92
00:06:21.875 --> 00:06:24.541
<b>such people, make the mistake of </b>
<b>staying on the surface, </b>

93
00:06:24.541 --> 00:06:31.125
<b>considering customs, rituals, </b>
<b>and ceremonies alone as religion.</b>

94
00:06:31.125 --> 00:06:35.916
<b>How can consciousness be fully purified this way?</b>

95
00:06:35.916 --> 00:06:40.000
<b>This raises two problems:</b>

96
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.166
<b>First</b>

97
00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:43.291
<b>Influenced by such people,</b>

98
00:06:43.291 --> 00:06:44.791
<b>others too</b>

99
00:06:44.791 --> 00:06:46.583
<b>without truly understanding,</b>

100
00:06:46.583 --> 00:06:50.958
<b>begin to consider mere religious </b>
<b>ceremonies as religion.</b>

101
00:06:50.958 --> 00:06:53.083
<b>Second</b>

102
00:06:53.083 --> 00:06:55.458
<b>These people appear religious, </b>

103
00:06:55.458 --> 00:06:58.000
<b>yet their minds remain disturbed.</b>

104
00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.375
<b>For instance,</b>

105
00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:01.166
<b>anger still arises,</b>

106
00:07:01.166 --> 00:07:03.750
<b>greed still torments.</b>

107
00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:09.541
<b>Seeing such people, others form </b>
<b>misconceptions about religion,</b>

108
00:07:09.541 --> 00:07:14.125
<b>beginning to view religious activities</b>
<b>as mere showmanship.</b>

109
00:07:14.125 --> 00:07:15.041
<b>Because</b>

110
00:07:15.041 --> 00:07:22.875
<b>the person practicing all this still </b>
<b>hasn't achieved inner purity.</b>

111
00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:30.416
<b>From both social and personal perspectives, </b>
<b>these three points are essential:</b>

112
00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:34.083
<b>Understand the true knowledge </b>
<b>and meaning of religion.</b>

113
00:07:34.083 --> 00:07:36.541
<b>Know its essence.</b>

114
00:07:36.541 --> 00:07:39.125
<b>For only personal gains!</b>

115
00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:42.958
<b>Don't chase religion merely for personal gains.</b>

116
00:07:42.958 --> 00:07:44.625
<b>And be vigilant</b>

117
00:07:44.625 --> 00:07:46.791
<b>without complete knowledge</b>

118
00:07:46.791 --> 00:07:50.541
<b>never mislead others.</b>

119
00:07:54.875 --> 00:08:01.875
<b>Many seek religion's shelter </b>
<b>solely for personal gain.</b>

120
00:08:01.875 --> 00:08:04.541
<b>They perform religious rituals.</b>

121
00:08:04.541 --> 00:08:08.708
<b>They receive some minor benefits,</b>

122
00:08:08.708 --> 00:08:12.125
<b>but due to this narrow mindset,</b>

123
00:08:12.125 --> 00:08:17.375
<b>they miss out on religion's true benefits.</b>

124
00:08:17.375 --> 00:08:21.375
<b>The same happens in professional life.</b>

125
00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:28.041
<b>Many people are motivated in their work only </b>
<b>when they receive high positions,</b>

126
00:08:28.041 --> 00:08:30.375
<b>increased salary,</b>

127
00:08:30.375 --> 00:08:33.000
<b>cars, and houses.</b>

128
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:38.291
<b>Now you might ask, what's wrong with that?</b>

129
00:08:38.291 --> 00:08:41.166
<b>And you'd be right to ask.</b>

130
00:08:41.166 --> 00:08:46.291
<b>Because desiring higher positions</b>
<b> or better pay isn't wrong.</b>

131
00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:50.375
<b>This is indeed a very natural </b>
<b>part of professional life.</b>

132
00:08:50.375 --> 00:08:51.166
<b>However, </b>

133
00:08:51.166 --> 00:08:53.625
<b>the problem arises</b>

134
00:08:53.625 --> 00:08:59.583
<b>when we make these our supreme purpose.</b>

135
00:08:59.583 --> 00:09:05.583
<b>In doing so, we overlook</b>
<b>these crucial questions:</b>

136
00:09:05.583 --> 00:09:09.708
<b>How is our work contributing to society?</b>

137
00:09:09.708 --> 00:09:16.375
<b>How are we improving others' lives by </b>
<b>teaching them something?</b>

138
00:09:16.375 --> 00:09:25.625
<b>Does the work we're doing align</b>
<b>with our values and nature?</b>

139
00:09:25.625 --> 00:09:35.083
<b>When we chase only position and salary, </b>
<b>forgetting this self-reflection,</b>

140
00:09:35.083 --> 00:09:38.083
<b>we gradually become exhausted.</b>

141
00:09:38.083 --> 00:09:39.416
<b>This is why</b>

142
00:09:39.416 --> 00:09:48.083
<b>you see many people around you who </b>
<b>have position, prestige, and money,</b>

143
00:09:48.083 --> 00:09:52.083
<b>yet aren't happy.</b>

144
00:09:52.083 --> 00:09:58.666
<b>Perhaps because they never reflected </b>
<b>on their work's deeper purpose,</b>

145
00:09:58.666 --> 00:10:04.958
<b>never considered its connection to inner peace.</b>

146
00:10:04.958 --> 00:10:10.750
<b>Your work is far beyond salary and position.</b>

147
00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.583
<b>Understand this truth.</b>

